-And the problem --

00:09:53.225 --> 00:09:58.263
the problem with dressing up
as Colonel Mustard stains

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:03.402
is that it's the only person
whose costume has a smell.

00:10:03.469 --> 00:10:07.373
So I'm just the guy at the party
who smells like mustard.

00:10:07.439 --> 00:10:08.740
Like at first they're like,

00:10:08.807 --> 00:10:10.542
oh, that's cute, Colonel Mustard
stains.

00:10:10.609 --> 00:10:13.612
And then you smell like mustard.

00:10:13.679 --> 00:10:18.284
And I was a little drunk,
so I was the guy who was drunk

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:23.222
and smells like mustard
at Questlove's party.

00:10:23.289 --> 00:10:27.593
And I don't usually
get drunk, but --

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:32.764
but we were playing Jenga,
and I kept losing at Jenga.

00:10:32.831 --> 00:10:37.235
And the penalty for losing
is you have to take a shot.

00:10:37.302 --> 00:10:42.674
And so I had like four shots,
and so I was the guy --

00:10:42.741 --> 00:10:46.278
My wife is like, Jenny was like
I've never seen you this drunk.

00:10:46.344 --> 00:10:48.713
Like, I was just the person
who was just like,

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:51.851
"Does anyone want to play
Jenga?!" You know what I mean?

00:10:51.917 --> 00:10:55.921
Like, I was that guy who also
smelled like mustard.

00:10:55.988 --> 00:10:59.491
And -- and so --

00:10:59.558 --> 00:11:02.627
So you know how when,
like, when you're drinking,

00:11:02.694 --> 00:11:05.464
you end up saying things
you're embarrassed about

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:07.866
and having really
strong opinions.

00:11:07.933 --> 00:11:09.868
So I had really strong opinions

00:11:09.935 --> 00:11:14.106
about people
who were at the party,

00:11:14.172 --> 00:11:16.642
because there's a lot
of famous people there.

00:11:16.708 --> 00:11:19.478
So like, for example,
like maybe I'd be talking

00:11:19.544 --> 00:11:21.680
if I were drunk about
like the movie "The Wrestler."

00:11:21.747 --> 00:11:23.015
But like Darren Aronofsky,

00:11:23.081 --> 00:11:25.083
who directed "The Wrestler,"
was at the party.

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:27.186
So I went over to him
and I was like,

00:11:27.252 --> 00:11:30.822
"Hey, why does the wrestler
have to die

00:11:30.889 --> 00:11:32.925
at the end of "The Wrestler?"

00:11:32.992 --> 00:11:35.260
[ Laughter ]

00:11:35.327 --> 00:11:38.697
And that didn't go well,
because --

00:11:38.764 --> 00:11:40.966
I know.
I was just -- it was terrible.

00:11:41.032 --> 00:11:42.668
-I've never even seen you drunk.
-No, I know.

00:11:42.735 --> 00:11:44.369
-But you're dressed as this guy.

00:11:44.436 --> 00:11:45.637
-And I'm dressed as that guy,
and I'm like...

00:11:45.704 --> 00:11:46.838
-Yelling at Darren Aronofsky.

00:11:46.905 --> 00:11:48.206
-...why does the wrestler
have to die

00:11:48.273 --> 00:11:49.708
at the end of "The Wrestler?"

00:11:49.775 --> 00:11:52.144
And then he was like, you know,
he had a really good answer.

00:11:52.211 --> 00:11:54.646
He's like -- he's like,
you know, he died

00:11:54.713 --> 00:11:57.850
so that we as the viewer
don't have to die.

00:11:57.916 --> 00:11:59.184
We can experience it.

00:11:59.251 --> 00:12:00.518
I was like, oh,
that's what "The Old Man

00:12:00.585 --> 00:12:02.087
and The Pool" is about.

00:12:02.154 --> 00:12:04.189
And I told him about "The Old
Man and The Pool."

00:12:04.256 --> 00:12:05.524
Yeah, yeah.
"Old Man and the Pool," yeah.

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:07.192
-But yeah.

00:12:07.258 --> 00:12:11.296
So anyway, here's my sentimental
Thanksgiving thing.

00:12:11.363 --> 00:12:15.067
I'll say -- it's like it's
things are hard right now.

00:12:15.134 --> 00:12:17.536
It's like a hard time.
People are having a hard time.

00:12:17.602 --> 00:12:21.706
This special, it's about being
alive and it's about mortality,

00:12:21.773 --> 00:12:23.842
and it's about bonding
with people you love.

00:12:23.909 --> 00:12:27.645
And I recommend it to people
who are age 12 to 112.

00:12:27.712 --> 00:12:29.781
Like, I'm really proud of it.
I hope people like it.

00:12:29.848 --> 00:12:31.983
-It's great for
the whole family.

00:12:32.050 --> 00:12:33.319
It really is great.

00:12:33.385 --> 00:12:35.921
And congratulations.
Dude, no one works harder.

00:12:35.988 --> 00:12:39.058
No one. I can't believe
I watched you make this.

00:12:39.125 --> 00:12:40.793
I'm so honored
to be your friend.

00:12:40.859 --> 00:12:42.293
I want to show a clip.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.396
Here's Mike Birbiglia
in "The Old Man and The Pool."

00:12:44.463 --> 00:12:45.765
Take a look.

00:12:45.831 --> 00:12:47.732
-We would recommend
you move out immediately

00:12:47.799 --> 00:12:49.434
until this is resolved.

00:12:49.501 --> 00:12:55.841
So we move into an Airbnb,
which, by the way, no breakfast.

00:12:55.908 --> 00:12:58.310
Which is one of the letters.

00:12:58.377 --> 00:13:01.480
[ Laughter ]

00:13:06.652 --> 00:13:09.788
This is a wildly
misleading acronym.

00:13:09.855 --> 00:13:12.190
It's like if you showed up
to an AA meeting

00:13:12.257 --> 00:13:18.597
and they were like, we're live
streaming and you're like.

00:13:18.664 --> 00:13:22.501
I had heard it was sort of
a private thing,

00:13:22.568 --> 00:13:24.502
and they're like,
pop open a wine cooler.

00:13:24.569 --> 00:13:27.939
We're going to dish some goss.

00:13:28.006 --> 00:13:30.042
-Dish some goss.
-We're gonna dish some goss.

00:13:30.109 --> 00:13:32.444
Get the family to watch it.
Mike Birbiglia, everybody.

00:13:32.511 --> 00:13:34.313
"The Old Man and The Pool"
is streaming

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:35.481
now on Netflix.

